## 4. FORMATTING

### Indentation
🔴 **4 spaces. Never tabs.**

### Braces
🔴 **Allman style — opening brace on new line:**
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
public void MyMethod()
{
    if (condition)
    {
        DoSomething();
    }
}

// ❌ Wrong
public void MyMethod() {
    if (condition) {
        DoSomething();
    }
}
```

### Control flow braces
🔴 **Always use braces for `if/else/for/while/foreach` unless single-line `if` without `else`:**
```csharp
// ✅ Correct — with else: always braces
if (condition)
{
    DoSomething();
}
else
{
    DoSomethingElse();
}

// ✅ Allowed — single-line if, no else
if (condition) DoSomething();

// ❌ Wrong — no braces with else
if (condition)
    DoSomething();
else
    DoSomethingElse();
```

### Spaces
🔴 **Spaces around operators and after commas/semicolons:**
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
int sum = a + b * 10;
if (score >= 100 && lives < 3) { }
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)
{
    CallMethod(arg1, arg2, arg3);
}

// ❌ Wrong
int sum=a+b*10;
for(int i=0;i<10;i++) { CallMethod(arg1,arg2,arg3); }
```

### Empty lines
🔴 **One empty line between methods.**  
🔴 **One empty line between class declarations.**  
🟡 **Empty line between logical sections inside a method.**

```csharp
public void MethodOne()
{
    // implementation
}

public void MethodTwo()
{
    int a = 10;
    string s = "test";

    DoSomethingWithVariables(a, s);

    if (condition)
    {
        // ...
    }
}
```

### Line length
🟡 **~100 characters max.** Break after comma or operator for long expressions.

