## 7. UNITY-SPECIFIC RULES

### MonoBehaviour Lifecycle
🔴 **Remove empty lifecycle methods** (`Start`, `Update`, `OnEnable`, etc.) — they cost CPU per object.

🔴 **Unity null check — use `if (obj != null)`, NEVER `obj?.Method()`:**
```csharp
// ✅ Correct — handles Unity's fake-null
if (enemy != null)
{
    enemy.Attack();
}

// ❌ Wrong — misses UnityEngine.Object fake-null
enemy?.Attack();
```

🟡 **Prefer events/subscriptions over `Update()` polling.**

🟡 **Explicit execution order with `[DefaultExecutionOrder]`:**
```csharp
[DefaultExecutionOrder(-100)]
public class ServicesInitializer : MonoBehaviour { }

[DefaultExecutionOrder(100)]
public class GameStarter : MonoBehaviour { }
```

### Component Access
🔴 **Cache `GetComponent` calls in `Awake()`. Never call in `Update()`:**
```csharp
private Rigidbody _rigidbody;

private void Awake()
{
    _rigidbody = GetComponent<Rigidbody>();
}

private void Update()
{
    _rigidbody.AddForce(Vector3.up); // ✅ uses cache
}
```

🔴 **`OnValidate()` for Editor-time auto-assignment only (no complex logic):**
```csharp
private void OnValidate()
{
    if (_animator == null)
    {
        _animator = GetComponent<Animator>();
    }
}
```

### DOTween
🔴 **Always cache tweens. Kill before starting new. Kill in `OnDestroy`:**
```csharp
private Sequence _fadeSequence;

public void AnimateFade()
{
    if (_fadeSequence != null)
    {
        _fadeSequence.Kill();
        _fadeSequence = null;
    }

    _fadeSequence = DOTween.Sequence();
    _fadeSequence.Append(canvasGroup.DOFade(0, 1f));
    _fadeSequence.Append(canvasGroup.DOFade(1, 1f));
}

private void OnDestroy()
{
    if (_fadeSequence != null)
    {
        _fadeSequence.Kill();
        _fadeSequence = null;
    }
}
```

> **KBPro shortcut:** Use `_seq = _seq.MakeSequence(gameObject)` and `tween.SafeKill()` — KBPro extension methods that handle null-safe Kill automatically.

### Coroutines
🔴 **Save coroutine reference. Stop in `OnDestroy`:**
```csharp
private Coroutine _movementCoroutine;

public void StartMovement()
{
    if (_movementCoroutine != null)
    {
        StopCoroutine(_movementCoroutine);
    }
    _movementCoroutine = StartCoroutine(MovementRoutine());
}

private void OnDestroy()
{
    if (_movementCoroutine != null)
    {
        StopCoroutine(_movementCoroutine);
    }
}
```

🟢 **Prefer `async/await` (UniTask) over coroutines for complex sequences:**
```csharp
public async UniTaskVoid LoadLevelAsync()
{
    isLoading = true;
    await SceneManager.LoadSceneAsync("Level1").ToUniTask();
    await InitializeGameState();
    isLoading = false;
}
```

### UnityEvent
🔴 **NEVER use `UnityEvent`. Use standard C# events or KBPro EventBus:**
```csharp
// ❌ FORBIDDEN
[SerializeField] private UnityEvent _onComplete;

// ✅ Correct — C# event
public event Action OnComplete;

// ✅ Correct — KBPro EventBus
EventBus<EventGameEnd>.Raise(new EventGameEnd { Result = GameResult.Victory });
```

### Addressables
🔴 **Use Addressables instead of `Resources.Load`:**
```csharp
// ✅
AsyncOperationHandle<GameObject> handle =
    Addressables.LoadAssetAsync<GameObject>($"enemies/{enemyId}");
await handle.ToUniTask();

// ❌
Resources.Load<GameObject>($"Enemies/{enemyId}");
```

🟡 **Release handles in `OnDestroy`:**
```csharp
private void OnDestroy()
{
    if (_enemyHandle.IsValid())
    {
        Addressables.Release(_enemyHandle);
    }
}
```

