## 10. CODING PATTERNS

### Magic numbers & strings
🔴 **No magic numbers or strings. Use named constants or enums:**
```csharp
// ❌
player.TakeDamage(10f);
_animator.Play("Run");

// ✅
private const float BULLET_DAMAGE = 10f;
player.TakeDamage(BULLET_DAMAGE);

// ✅ KBPro way — use Constants class or [ConstSelector]
_animator.Play(Constants.SPINESYSTEMID.RUN);
```

### Event unsubscription
🟡 **Always unsubscribe on `OnDisable` or `Dispose`:**
```csharp
private void OnEnable()
{
    GameEvents.LevelComplete += HandleLevelComplete;
}

private void OnDisable()
{
    GameEvents.LevelComplete -= HandleLevelComplete; // MANDATORY
}
```

### SOLID
🔴 **Follow SRP** — one class/method = one responsibility.  
🔴 **Follow ISP** — small focused interfaces over fat ones.

### DRY / KISS / YAGNI
🟢 **DRY** — extract repeated logic to shared methods.  
🟢 **KISS** — prefer simple solutions. No premature abstraction.  
🟢 **YAGNI** — don't write code "just in case."

