## 12. KBPRO-SPECIFIC PATTERNS (DO NOT IGNORE)

These patterns are **project-defined** and take priority over generic Unity conventions.

```csharp
// ✅ Service access — ALWAYS via LazySrv
private LazySrv<IStatisticService> _statService = new();
// Usage: _statService.Value.GetValue<T>(key)

// ✅ Event subscription
private EventBinding<EventGameEnd> _onGameEnd;
void Init()
{
    _onGameEnd = new EventBinding<EventGameEnd>(OnGameEnd);
    EventBus<EventGameEnd>.Register(_onGameEnd);
}
void Dispose()
{
    EventBus<EventGameEnd>.Unregister(_onGameEnd); // ALWAYS unregister
}

// ✅ Sound play/stop — always use null-safe extensions
_music?.SafePlay();
_music?.SafeStop();

// ✅ DOTween with KBPro utils
_seq = _seq.MakeSequence(gameObject);
_seq.Append(...).OnComplete(OnDone);
// No need to null-check — MakeSequence handles it

// ✅ No magic strings — use Constants class
EventBus<EventShowComponent>.Raise(
    new EventShowComponent(Constants.UICOMPONENT.SETTINGS));

// ✅ String fields with [ConstSelector] attribute
[SerializeField, ConstSelector("Audio_SFX")]
private string _soundId;

// ✅ Async — always UniTask, always with CancellationToken when inside module
public async UniTask DoAsync(CancellationToken ct)
{
    await UniTask.WaitUntil(() => _isReady, cancellationToken: ct);
}
```

---

## QUICK REFERENCE: DO / DON'T

| DO | DON'T |
|----|-------|
| `private LazySrv<T> _srv = new()` | `ServiceLocator.GetService<T>()` in logic |
| `EventBus<T>.Raise(new T())` | Direct method calls between modules |
| `_sound.SafePlay()` | `_sound.Play()` (not null-safe) |
| `tween.SafeKill()` or `MakeSequence()` | Naked `DOTween.Kill()` without null check |
| `[SerializeField] private X _x = null` | `public X x;` as inspector field |
| `Constants.UICOMPONENT.GAME` | `"Game"` as string literal |
| `if (obj != null)` | `obj?.Method()` for Unity objects |
| Unsubscribe in `Dispose()` | Leave events subscribed on destroy |
| `base.Dispose()` last in Dispose chain | Skip base calls in lifecycle overrides |
| `// NOTE:` for intentional rule breaks | Silent rule violations |
